# Specific names

Name a file, a config section, and an exported symbol after the agent that owns it or the task it performs. A generic label does not say which agent or which task.

The path can carry the agent when the file already lives inside that agent. The identifier still has to name the task.

```json
// Bad: the section could belong to any word count
{ "lessThanWords": { "enabled": true, "words": 6 } }

// Good: this section counts words in the orchestrator input
{ "lessThanInputWords": { "enabled": true, "words": 6, "print": true } }
```

```text
src/utils.ts
src/helper.ts
src/less-than-six.ts
```

```text
src/less-than-input-words.ts
extensions/less-than-input-words/index.ts
```

Fields inside a task section stay short (`enabled`, `words`, `print`). The section around them is what must name the task.
